#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/05_uskok_and_the_doge/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The letters of his friends spoke for him before the Doge's council."
msgstr "Письма друзей замолвили за него слово перед советом дожа."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/05_uskok_and_the_doge/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Juraj is home in Senj again."
msgstr "Юрай снова дома, в Сене."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, a fever spreads in the villages around the Bay of Kotor!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, в деревнях у Которского залива ходит лихорадка!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Only Doctor Marin of Ragusa knows how to stop it."
msgstr "Только доктор Марин из Рагузы знает, как её остановить."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He goes from patient to patient along the coast. Find him!"
msgstr "Он ходит от больного к больному вдоль берега. {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} его!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The doctor wore {hallmark}."
msgstr "Доктора легко узнать: у него {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen Doctor Marin?"
msgstr "Вы видели доктора Марина?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, visiting a patient! But which one is the doctor?"
msgstr "Он здесь, у больного! Но кто из них доктор?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Doctor Marin?"
msgstr "Кто из них доктор Марин?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the doctor! Remember what the people told you."
msgstr ""
"Нет, это не доктор! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните}, что {crew|тебе|тебе|вам} рассказали люди."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"\"Kotor needs me? Then hurry to the apothecary of the Franciscans in Dubrovnik for my medicine!\""
msgstr ""
"«Я нужен Котору? Тогда {crew|спеши|спеши|спешите} в аптеку францисканцев в Дубровнике за моим "
"лекарством!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Doctor Marin sent you? Here is the medicine, made by our brothers."
msgstr "{crew|Тебя|Тебя|Вас} прислал доктор Марин? Вот лекарство, его сделали наши братья."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hurry to Kotor, and steer carefully through the narrow strait!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Спеши|Спеши|Спешите} в Котор и осторожно {crew|проходи|проходи|проходите} узкий пролив!"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fetch the medicine."
msgstr "{crew|Забери|Забери|Заберите} лекарство."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the medicine to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} лекарство {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The medicine! Thank you, captain!"
msgstr "Лекарство! Спасибо, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now our children will get well again."
msgstr "Теперь наши дети снова поправятся."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fever is gone from the Bay of Kotor!"
msgstr "Лихорадка ушла из Которского залива!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The bells of St. Tryphon ring for you, captain."
msgstr "Колокола святого Трифона звонят для {crew|тебя, капитан|тебя, капитан|вас, капитаны}."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Doctor of Ragusa"
msgstr "Доктор из Рагузы"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A fever spreads around the Bay of Kotor. Find Doctor Marin and bring his medicine."
msgstr ""
"У Которского залива ходит лихорадка. {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} доктора Марина и "
"{crew|привези|привези|привезите} его лекарство."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In 1377, Ragusa was the first city to keep travellers apart for a while before they could enter: a"
" quarantine, against the illnesses. The pharmacy of the Franciscans in Dubrovnik, from 1317, still"
" sells medicine today."
msgstr ""
"В 1377 году Рагуза первой стала ненадолго держать путников отдельно, прежде чем впустить в город: "
"так появился карантин, защита от болезней. Аптека францисканцев в Дубровнике работает с 1317 года "
"и продаёт лекарства до сих пор."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The fever is gone!"
msgstr "Лихорадки больше нет!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Doctor Marin's medicine reached Kotor just in time."
msgstr "Лекарство доктора Марина прибыло в Котор как раз вовремя."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/06_doctor_of_ragusa/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The children of the bay are well again."
msgstr "Дети залива снова здоровы."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, Hvar opens a theatre for everybody, rich and poor!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, на Хваре открывается театр для всех, для богатых и бедных!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But the Aga's men scared my actors away, all along the coast."
msgstr "Но люди Аги разогнали моих актёров по всему побережью."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find them and bring them to Hvar before the opening night!"
msgstr ""
"{crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} их и {crew|привези|привези|привезите} на Хвар до вечера премьеры!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's men said a jester is a useless man."
msgstr "Люди Аги сказали, что шут — бесполезный человек."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ha! I will make all of Hvar laugh."
msgstr "Ха! Я рассмешу весь Хвар."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I hid in the cathedral and sang to the stone heads."
msgstr "Я пряталась в соборе и пела каменным головам."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now I will sing for real people again!"
msgstr "Теперь я снова буду петь для живых людей!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Old Toma never misses an opening night."
msgstr "Старый Тома никогда не пропускает премьеру."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I have a new story about a clever captain..."
msgstr ""
"У меня есть новая история {crew|о хитроумном капитане|о хитроумном капитане|о хитроумных "
"капитанах}..."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Find {count} more {count|actor|actors}."
msgstr "{crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} ещё {count} {count|актёра|актёров|актёров}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the actors to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} актёров {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pero! Go and put on your bells."
msgstr "Перо! Иди надевай свои бубенцы."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Dora! Your voice will fill the whole hall."
msgstr "Дора! Твой голос наполнит весь зал."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Toma! Now we have all our actors."
msgstr "Тома! Теперь все наши актёры здесь."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The curtain rises!"
msgstr "Занавес поднимается!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fishermen and nobles sit side by side, and everybody laughs."
msgstr "Рыбаки и знать сидят бок о бок, и все смеются."

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Theatre of Hvar"
msgstr "Театр Хвара"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's men scared the actors away. Bring them to Hvar for the opening of the theatre."
msgstr "Люди Аги разогнали актёров. {crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} их на Хвар к открытию театра."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hvar's theatre opened in 1612 above the town's galley shed. It is one of the oldest public "
"theatres in Europe, paid for by the town for all the people of Hvar."
msgstr ""
"Театр Хвара открылся в 1612 году над городским арсеналом для галер. Это один из старейших "
"публичных театров Европы, и город построил его для всех жителей Хвара."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The theatre is full!"
msgstr "Театр полон!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The jester, the singer and the storyteller made it to Hvar."
msgstr "Шут, певица и сказочник добрались до Хвара."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/07_theatre_of_hvar/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The whole town laughs, sings and listens together."
msgstr "Весь город вместе смеётся, поёт и слушает."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome, captain. The villages have written down everything the Aga did."
msgstr "Добро пожаловать, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}. Деревни записали всё, что сделал Ага."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring their complaint to the envoy of the Pope in Ancona."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} их жалобу посланнику папы в Анкону."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is my letter of recommendation. Cross the sea, and may the wind be kind!"
msgstr ""
"Вот моё рекомендательное письмо. {crew|Переплыви|Переплыви|Переплывите} море — попутного "
"{crew|тебе|тебе|вам} ветра!"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the complaint across the sea to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} жалобу за море, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A complaint about an aga? Let me read it."
msgstr "Жалоба на агу? {crew|Дай-ка|Дай-ка|Дайте-ка} прочитать."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which emperor's arch stands at our harbour?"
msgstr "Арка какого императора стоит у нашей гавани?"

#. an answer on a button, a few words
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The arch of Trajan"
msgstr "Арка Траяна"

#. an answer on a button, a few words
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The arch of Diocletian"
msgstr "Арка Диоклетиана"

#. an answer on a button, a few words
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The arch of the Doge"
msgstr "Арка дожа"

#. what a judge says before the questions, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But first, tell me: are you really sailors who know our sea?"
msgstr ""
"Но сначала {crew|скажи: ты правда знаешь|скажи: ты правда знаешь|скажите: вы правда знаете} наше "
"море?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Hmm, no. Look around the harbour, and think again!"
msgstr ""
"Хм, нет. {crew|Оглядись в гавани и подумай|Оглядись в гавани и подумай|Оглядитесь в гавани и "
"подумайте} ещё!"

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Right! You know our sea."
msgstr "Верно! {crew|Ты знаешь|Ты знаешь|Вы знаете} наше море."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But only the Viceroy's man in Bari can carry this to the court of the Sultan."
msgstr "Но только человек вице-короля в Бари может передать это ко двору султана."

#. what a judge says after the right answers, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sail to the town where they keep the bones of St. Nicholas!"
msgstr "{crew|Плыви|Плыви|Плывите} в город, где хранятся мощи святого Николая!"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the complaint to the Viceroy's man in {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} жалобу человеку вице-короля {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The envoy of the Pope sends you? Then it is serious."
msgstr "{crew|Тебя|Тебя|Вас} прислал посланник папы? Значит, дело серьёзное."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take my sealed answer back to the Rector of Ragusa."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} мой запечатанный ответ ректору Рагузы."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the sealed answer back to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} запечатанный ответ обратно {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The answer from Bari! Let me break the seal..."
msgstr "Ответ из Бари! Сейчас сломаю печать..."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Aga shall be heard before a judge.\""
msgstr "«Ага предстанет перед судьёй»."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the villages will have their day in court!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, деревни добьются суда!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Across the Sea"
msgstr "За море"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the villages' complaint across the sea to Ancona and Bari."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} жалобу деревень за море, в Анкону и Бари."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The bones of St. Nicholas, the saint of the sailors and of the children, were brought to Bari by "
"its sailors in 1087."
msgstr ""
"Мощи святого Николая, покровителя моряков и детей, привезли в Бари моряки этого города в 1087 "
"году."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You crossed the sea!"
msgstr "{crew|Ты переплыл|Ты переплыла|Вы переплыли} море!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The complaint reached the Pope's envoy and the Viceroy."
msgstr "Жалоба дошла до посланника папы и до вице-короля."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/08_across_the_sea/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga will have to face a judge."
msgstr "Аге придётся предстать перед судьёй."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, pilgrims from Ragusa came to Bari to see St. Nicholas."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, паломники из Рагузы приплыли в Бари поклониться святому Николаю."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But the Aga's men took the money for their passage home."
msgstr "Но люди Аги отобрали у них деньги на дорогу домой."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take them home across the sea! But first, find little Luka, who ran off along the coast."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} их домой через море! Но сначала {crew|найди|найди|найдите} "
"маленького Луку: он сбежал куда-то вдоль берега."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Luka has {hallmark}."
msgstr "У Луки {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen Luka, a ship's boy from Ragusa?"
msgstr "Вы видели Луку, юнгу из Рагузы?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Luka is here, with the ship's boys of the harbour! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Лука здесь, с юнгами порта! Но который из них он?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Luka? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr "Который из них Лука? {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните}, что {crew|тебе|тебе|вам} рассказали!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not Luka! Think of everything you heard."
msgstr ""
"Нет, это не Лука! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} всё, что {crew|ты слышал|ты слышала|вы "
"слышали}."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I only wanted to see the sea of Italy! Take me home, please.\""
msgstr ""
"«Я только хотел посмотреть на море Италии! {crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} меня домой, пожалуйста»."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the pilgrims and Luka home to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} паломников и Луку домой, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims are home! Thank you, captain."
msgstr "Паломники дома! Спасибо, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring Luka home to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} Луку домой, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Luka! There you are!"
msgstr "Лука! Вот ты где!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims will tell everybody about the kind captain."
msgstr "Паломники всем расскажут {crew|о добром капитане|о добром капитане|о добрых капитанах}."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And Luka? He wants to become a captain, too!"
msgstr "А Лука? Он тоже хочет стать капитаном!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Pilgrims of St. Nicholas"
msgstr "Паломники святого Николая"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga's men took the pilgrims' money. Find little Luka and take them all home across the sea."
msgstr ""
"Люди Аги отобрали деньги у паломников. {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} маленького Луку и "
"{crew|отвези|отвези|отвезите} всех домой через море."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The whole floor of Otranto cathedral is one huge mosaic, made in the 1160s by artists led by a "
"monk called Pantaleon, with a great Tree of Life running along it."
msgstr ""
"Весь пол собора в Отранто — одна огромная мозаика. Её сделали в 1160-х годах мастера под началом "
"монаха Панталеона, и по ней тянется большое Древо жизни."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The pilgrims are home!"
msgstr "Паломники дома!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You found Luka and took the pilgrims home across the sea."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ты нашёл|Ты нашла|Вы нашли} Луку и {crew|отвёз|отвезла|отвезли} паломников домой через море."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/09_pilgrims_of_st_nicholas/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "In Ragusa, the bells ring for them."
msgstr "В Рагузе для них звонят колокола."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! The corsairs of Ulcinj took all our olive oil."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}! Корсары из Улциня забрали всё наше оливковое масло."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "We traded it for the winter, and now we have nothing."
msgstr "Мы выменяли его, чтобы хватило на зиму, а теперь у нас ничего нет."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Nobody fights them. Go and ask what they want for it!"
msgstr ""
"Драться с ними никто не станет. {crew|Сходи|Сходи|Сходите} и {crew|спроси|спроси|спросите}, чего "
"они за него хотят!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oil for oil? No, no. My sail is torn to rags."
msgstr "Масло за масло? Нет-нет. Мой парус порван в клочья."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a new sail, and you get your oil back."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Принеси|Принеси|Принесите} мне новый парус — и {crew|получишь|получишь|получите} своё масло "
"обратно."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The sailmaker of Durrës makes the best sails."
msgstr "Лучшие паруса шьёт парусный мастер из Дурреса."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A new sail! Fine work. Here is your oil, captain."
msgstr ""
"Новый парус! Отличная работа. Вот {crew|твоё|твоё|ваше} масло, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "And tell the Aga that Crooked Mast is not his friend."
msgstr "И {crew|передай|передай|передайте} Аге, что Кривая Мачта ему не друг."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A sail? Gladly, but my cough is so bad, I can not work."
msgstr "Парус? С радостью, но я так сильно кашляю, что не могу работать."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Only the honey of Vlorë helps."
msgstr "Помогает только мёд из Влёры."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me a jar of honey!"
msgstr "{crew|Принеси|Принеси|Принесите} мне горшочек мёда!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey from Vlorë! My cough is gone already."
msgstr "Мёд из Влёры! Кашель уже прошёл."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is the sail. The finest in the Adriatic!"
msgstr "Вот парус. Лучший на Адриатике!"

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey? My bees made plenty."
msgstr "Мёд? Его у меня много: пчёлы постарались."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But I need salt for my cheese. Do you have salt on board?"
msgstr "Но мне нужна соль для сыра. У {crew|тебя|тебя|вас} есть соль на борту?"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt! Just what I needed."
msgstr "Соль! Как раз то, что мне нужно."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Here is a jar of my best honey."
msgstr "Вот горшочек моего лучшего мёда."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the olive oil home to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} оливковое масло домой, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Our oil! Now we have enough for the winter."
msgstr "Наше масло! Теперь нам хватит на зиму."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast sent a message, too:"
msgstr "Кривая Мачта тоже прислал весточку:"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"The Aga's scribe sails south with a heavy book. Watch out for him!\""
msgstr ""
"«Писарь Аги плывёт на юг с тяжёлой книгой. {crew|Высматривай|Высматривай|Высматривайте} его!»"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Corsairs of Ulcinj"
msgstr "Корсары Улциня"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The corsairs took the villages' olive oil. Find out what they want, and trade it back."
msgstr ""
"Корсары забрали оливковое масло деревень. {crew|Узнай|Узнай|Узнайте}, чего они хотят, и "
"{crew|выменяй|выменяй|выменяйте} его обратно."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The olive trees of the Adriatic grow very old: near Bar in Montenegro stands an olive tree which "
"is said to be more than two thousand years old."
msgstr ""
"Оливы на Адриатике живут очень долго: у города Бар в Черногории растёт олива, которой, говорят, "
"больше двух тысяч лет."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oil is home!"
msgstr "Масло дома!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Not a single shot was fired: a sail, a jar of honey and a sack of salt did it."
msgstr "Ни одного выстрела: всё сделали парус, горшочек мёда и мешок соли."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/10_corsairs_of_ulcinj/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Even the corsair captain is your friend now."
msgstr "Даже капитан корсаров теперь {crew|твой|твой|ваш} друг."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, Ага требует апельсины Парги в уплату налога!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eleni of Parga hid the harvest from his men."
msgstr "Элени из Парги спрятала урожай от его людей."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Help her get the oranges to the market of Corfu, so that the money stays with the people."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Помоги|Помоги|Помогите} ей доставить апельсины на рынок Корфу, чтобы деньги остались у "
"людей."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges are ripe, but the Aga's men broke all my baskets."
msgstr "Апельсины созрели, но люди Аги сломали все мои корзины."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring me baskets! Ilir of Vlorë weaves the best ones."
msgstr "{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} мне корзины! Лучшие плетёт Илир из Влёры."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Fine baskets! Here are the oranges, captain."
msgstr "Отличные корзины! Вот апельсины, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Smell them: the sun of Parga is inside."
msgstr "{crew|Понюхай|Понюхай|Понюхайте}: в них солнце Парги."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I weave baskets from the reeds of the lagoon."
msgstr "Я плету корзины из тростника лагуны."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "But my boat lost its rope. Spiros in Corfu has ropes!"
msgstr "Но моя лодка потеряла канат. У Спироса на Корфу есть канаты!"

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A good rope! Here are my baskets."
msgstr "Хороший канат! Вот мои корзины."

#. what a person in a chain of trades wants, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope for Ilir? The harbour of Corfu has ropes for everybody."
msgstr "Канат для Илира? В порту Корфу канаты есть для всех."

#. what a person says after a trade, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Take this one, captain."
msgstr "{crew|Бери|Бери|Берите} этот, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the oranges to the market of {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} апельсины на рынок, {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Oranges from Parga! The whole market smells of them."
msgstr "Апельсины из Парги! Весь рынок ими пахнет."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The money goes to the people of Parga, not to the Aga."
msgstr "Деньги достанутся жителям Парги, а не Аге."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every orange was sold, and Parga keeps its money."
msgstr "Все апельсины проданы, и деньги остались в Парге."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga gets only the peels!"
msgstr "Аге достанется только кожура!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Oranges of Parga"
msgstr "Апельсины Парги"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Aga wants the oranges of Parga as a tax. Trade your way to baskets and bring the oranges to "
"the market of Corfu."
msgstr ""
"Ага требует апельсины Парги в уплату налога. {crew|Выменяй|Выменяй|Выменяйте} корзины и "
"{crew|отвези|отвези|отвезите} апельсины на рынок Корфу."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Parga was a little Venetian town on the Greek coast for almost 400 years, with Ottoman lands all "
"around it, and it was often raided by its neighbours."
msgstr ""
"Парга почти 400 лет была маленьким венецианским городком на греческом берегу. Вокруг лежали "
"османские земли, и соседи часто на неё нападали."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Sweet oranges for Corfu!"
msgstr "Сладкие апельсины для Корфу!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The oranges reached the market, and the money stayed in Parga."
msgstr "Апельсины попали на рынок, а деньги остались в Парге."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/11_oranges_of_parga/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A rope, a basket and a lot of sailing did it."
msgstr "Всё решили канат, корзины и долгое плавание."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the warning of Crooked Mast came true!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, предупреждение Кривой Мачты сбылось!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe was here with a heavy book: the ledger of the double taxes."
msgstr "Писарь Аги был здесь с тяжёлой книгой: это книга двойных налогов."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "With it, we can prove everything. But he fled in a hurry. Chase him!"
msgstr "С ней мы всё докажем. Но он в спешке сбежал. {crew|Догони|Догони|Догоните} его!"

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The scribe had {hallmark}."
msgstr "Писаря легко узнать: у него {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen the Aga's scribe with a heavy book?"
msgstr "Вы видели писаря Аги с тяжёлой книгой?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "He is here, hiding among the people of the harbour! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Он здесь, прячется среди людей в гавани! Но кто же из них он?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is the Aga's scribe?"
msgstr "Кто из них писарь Аги?"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not the scribe! Remember all four things you learned."
msgstr "Нет, это не писарь! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} все четыре приметы."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Alright, alright! Here is the ledger. I only wrote what the Aga told me!\""
msgstr "«Ладно, ладно! Вот книга. Я только записывал то, что велел Ага!»"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"I will tell the truth before the judge, I promise.\""
msgstr "«Я скажу правду перед судьёй, обещаю»."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger proves it: the Aga took every tax twice!"
msgstr "Книга это доказывает: Ага брал каждый налог дважды!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Forged Ledger"
msgstr "Поддельная книга"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's scribe flees with the ledger of the double taxes. Chase him along the coast!"
msgstr ""
"Писарь Аги бежит с книгой двойных налогов. {crew|Догоняй|Догоняй|Догоняйте} его вдоль берега!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Spectacles were made in Venice from about 1300 on; the glassmakers of Murano were so precious that"
" they were not allowed to leave the republic."
msgstr ""
"Очки делали в Венеции примерно с 1300 года. Стеклодувы Мурано были так ценны, что им не разрешали "
"покидать республику."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The ledger is yours!"
msgstr "Книга у {crew|тебя|тебя|вас}!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "You chased the scribe along the whole coast and found him."
msgstr ""
"{crew|Ты гнался|Ты гналась|Вы гнались} за писарем вдоль всего берега и {crew|нашёл|нашла|нашли} "
"его."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/12_forged_ledger/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the crew holds the proof of the double taxes."
msgstr "Теперь у команды есть доказательство двойных налогов."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, I must confess something."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, я должен кое в чём признаться."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"I wrote the list of the villages in the old Glagolitic letters, so that the Aga could not read it."
msgstr "Я записал список деревень старой глаголицей, чтобы Ага не смог его прочитать."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now I can not read it either! Find a priest who knows the old letters."
msgstr ""
"А теперь и сам не могу его прочитать! {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} священника, который знает старые "
"буквы."

#. a clue; {hallmark} is a noun phrase like 'a patched red sail'
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The priest has {hallmark}."
msgstr "У священника {hallmark}."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Have you seen a priest who knows the old letters?"
msgstr "Вы видели священника, который знает старые буквы?"

#. a line in the last port of a trail
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur is here, at the market! But which one is he?"
msgstr "Дон Гргур здесь, на рынке! Но который из них он?"

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Which one is Don Grgur? Remember what the people told you!"
msgstr ""
"Который из них дон Гргур? {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните}, что {crew|тебе|тебе|вам} рассказали!"

#. a line after a wrong pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "No, that is not him! Think of all three things you learned."
msgstr "Нет, это не он! {crew|Вспомни|Вспомни|Вспомните} все три приметы."

#. a line after the right pick
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "\"Yes, I read the old letters. Let me see... every village, and every ducat!\""
msgstr "«Да, я читаю старые буквы. Посмотрим... каждая деревня и каждый дукат!»"

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the list back to the scribe in {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} список обратно писарю {port@in}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every village and every ducat, written clearly at last!"
msgstr "Каждая деревня и каждый дукат, наконец-то записаны ясно!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge can give back every coin."
msgstr "Теперь судья сможет вернуть каждую монету."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is ready for the judge."
msgstr "Список готов для судьи."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will never write in a secret script again!"
msgstr "Больше никогда не буду писать тайным письмом!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Secret Script"
msgstr "Тайное письмо"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The list of the villages is written in old Glagolitic letters. Find a priest who can read it."
msgstr ""
"Список деревень записан старой глаголицей. {crew|Найди|Найди|Найдите} священника, который сможет "
"его прочитать."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Glagolitic is the oldest known Slavic alphabet. On the islands of Kvarner, like Krk, and on the "
"islands near Zadar, Croatian priests and scribes kept writing in it for centuries."
msgstr ""
"Глаголица — самая древняя из известных славянских азбук. На островах Кварнера, например на Крке, и"
" на островах у Задара хорватские священники и писари писали ею веками."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The list is read!"
msgstr "Список прочитан!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Don Grgur read the old letters for you."
msgstr "Дон Гргур прочитал для {crew|тебя|тебя|вас} старые буквы."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/13_secret_script/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Now the judge will know every village and every ducat."
msgstr "Теперь судья будет знать каждую деревню и каждый дукат."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the judge wants to hear witnesses, not only the ledger."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, судье мало одной книги: он хочет выслушать свидетелей."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast in Ulcinj, Mustafa in Castelnuovo and Jele in Kotor saw what the Aga's men did."
msgstr "Кривая Мачта в Улцине, Мустафа в Кастельнуово и Йеле в Которе видели, что творили люди Аги."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring all three to Corfu, where the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} всех троих на Корфу, откуда начнётся путь к судье!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Me, a witness? Ha! Fine."
msgstr "Я — свидетель? Ха! Ладно."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I saw the Aga's men take a tax twice, right at sea."
msgstr "Я видел, как люди Аги брали налог дважды, прямо в море."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I keep the gate of Castelnuovo."
msgstr "Я стерегу ворота Кастельнуово."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Every cart of the Aga's men went through it, twice."
msgstr "Каждая повозка людей Аги проходила через них дважды."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "They took my olives as a tax, and came back a week later for more."
msgstr "Они забрали мои оливки как налог, а через неделю вернулись за новыми."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge everything."
msgstr "Я всё расскажу судье."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Pick up {count} more {count|witness|witnesses}."
msgstr "{crew|Забери|Забери|Заберите} ещё {count} {count|свидетеля|свидетелей|свидетелей}."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} свидетелей {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Crooked Mast? A corsair as a witness... the judge will be surprised!"
msgstr "Кривая Мачта? Корсар в свидетелях... судья удивится!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Mustafa, the gatekeeper. Welcome to Corfu!"
msgstr "Мустафа, привратник. Добро пожаловать на Корфу!"

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Jele of Kotor. Rest a little, the voyage is long."
msgstr "Йеле из Котора. Отдохните немного, путь долгий."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready, and so is the ledger."
msgstr "Свидетели готовы, и книга тоже."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Soon, the voyage to the judge begins!"
msgstr "Скоро начнётся путь к судье!"

#. the title of a mission, on its card
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Witnesses"
msgstr "Свидетели"

#. the summary of a mission, one or two short sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The judge wants to hear witnesses. Bring them from Ulcinj, Castelnuovo and Kotor to Corfu."
msgstr ""
"Судья хочет выслушать свидетелей. {crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} их из Улциня, Кастельнуово и "
"Котора на Корфу."

#. a fun fact at the end of a mission, at most three sentences
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The Republic of Ragusa banned the slave trade in 1416. It valued freedom very highly: the word "
"Libertas stands on its flag."
msgstr ""
"Республика Рагуза запретила работорговлю в 1416 году. Она очень ценила свободу: на её флаге "
"написано слово Libertas."

#. the headline of the screen at the end of a mission, a few words
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The witnesses are ready!"
msgstr "Свидетели готовы!"

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "A corsair, a gatekeeper and an olive grower will speak before the judge."
msgstr "Корсар, привратник и хозяйка оливковой рощи выступят перед судьёй."

#. what the crew achieved, on the screen at the end of a mission, one sentence
#: data/missions/14_the_witnesses/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Aga's days as a tax collector are numbered."
msgstr "Дни Аги как сборщика налогов сочтены."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain, the day has come!"
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}, этот день настал!"

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to the kadı of Preveza: he judges by the law."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} книгу и свидетелей к кадию Превезы: он судит по закону."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Master Ivan waits in Parga, and Doctor Marin is here in Corfu."
msgstr "Мастер Иван ждёт в Парге, а доктор Марин здесь, на Корфу."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I am ready, captain. I will tell the judge about the fever."
msgstr "Я готов, {crew|капитан|капитан|капитаны}. Я расскажу судье о лихорадке."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Captain! I came all the way from Pula."
msgstr "{crew|Капитан|Капитан|Капитаны}! Я приплыл из самой Пулы."

#. a line which a person says, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "I will tell the judge about the Aga's recruiter."
msgstr "Я расскажу судье о вербовщике Аги."

#. the objective while sailing, on the banner
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bring the ledger and the witnesses to {port}."
msgstr "{crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} книгу и свидетелей {port@to}."

#. a line of thanks, at most two short sentences
#: data/missions/15_kadi_of_preveza/mission.tres
#, fuzzy
msgid "Peace be with you. Show me the ledger, and let the witnesses speak."
msgstr ""
"Мир {crew|тебе|тебе|вам}. {crew|Покажи|Покажи|Покажите} мне книгу, и пусть говорят свидетели."

#. what the crew asks, or what the crew is asked
